1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:04,824
In a palace in Florence hangs a painting of the Virgin Mary.

2
00:00:04,824 --> 00:00:08,117
Over her shoulder floats a grey oval object.

3
00:00:08,117 --> 00:00:12,533
Below it, a man shields his eyes, and his dog looks up too.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,445
Online, that painting sits in a famous lineup.

5
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:19,891
A medieval fresco with two pilots in capsules.

6
00:00:19,891 --> 00:00:23,336
A German news sheet about a battle in the sky.

7
00:00:23,336 --> 00:00:26,033
Rock carvings of figures in helmets.

8
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:32,476
Ancient astronaut writers call it proof: artists recording visitors from somewhere else.

9
00:00:32,476 --> 00:00:37,366
So tonight we walk through a gallery of six of the most famous exhibits.

10
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:40,528
At every exhibit we ask three questions.

11
00:00:40,528 --> 00:00:42,212
What did the artist mean?

12
00:00:42,212 --> 00:00:45,513
Does the shape match the conventions of its time?

13
00:00:45,513 --> 00:00:48,410
And did anyone back then call it a machine?

14
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:50,566
Then a scorecard, and a verdict.

15
00:00:55,033 --> 00:00:56,793
One note before we enter.

16
00:00:56,793 --> 00:01:03,835
The images you will see are stylised reconstructions made for this video, not the original artworks.

17
00:01:03,835 --> 00:01:06,299
Every source is in the description.

18
00:01:06,766 --> 00:01:10,752
Room one: the Kimberley, in the far north-west of Australia.

19
00:01:10,752 --> 00:01:16,066
On its cliffs and cave walls are some of the most striking figures ever painted.

20
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:18,259
They are the Wandjina.

21
00:01:18,259 --> 00:01:22,651
Huge white faces, large dark eyes, a nose, but no mouth.

22
00:01:22,651 --> 00:01:25,946
Around each head runs a band of red lines.

23
00:01:25,946 --> 00:01:29,633
Some stretch five metres across a rock ceiling.

24
00:01:30,099 --> 00:01:35,917
In nineteen sixty-eight, Erich von Daniken used them in Chariots of the Gods.

25
00:01:35,917 --> 00:01:40,375
The band became a space helmet, the mouthless face a visor.

26
00:01:40,375 --> 00:01:43,699
Visitors from the stars, remembered on rock.

27
00:01:44,166 --> 00:01:47,016
The idea that outsiders made them is older.

28
00:01:47,016 --> 00:01:55,166
In eighteen thirty-eight, the explorer George Grey sketched Wandjina and doubted that local people could have painted them.

29
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:59,508
Now the art history, from the people whose art it is.

30
00:01:59,508 --> 00:02:05,942
The Wandjina are cloud and rain spirits of the Worrorra, Ngarinyin and Wunambal peoples.

31
00:02:05,942 --> 00:02:08,866
The lines around the head are lightning.

32
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:10,764
And the missing mouth?

33
00:02:10,764 --> 00:02:13,432
They are so powerful they need no speech.

34
00:02:13,432 --> 00:02:17,466
And if they had mouths, it is said, the rain would never stop.

35
00:02:17,933 --> 00:02:19,927
These are living paintings.

36
00:02:19,927 --> 00:02:26,647
The Mowanjum community repaints them to renew the Wandjina's presence and call the monsoon.

37
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:30,266
At one site, the paint is over forty layers deep.

38
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:38,147
The style appears around four thousand years ago, after a long drought gave way to regular monsoons.

39
00:02:38,147 --> 00:02:42,300
Rain spirits, arriving in the art as the rains returned.

40
00:02:42,766 --> 00:02:44,204
Exhibit one verdict.

41
00:02:44,204 --> 00:02:48,086
A helmet only if you ignore the people who paint them.

42
00:02:48,086 --> 00:02:53,550
Traditional owners have worked to reclaim the Wandjina from the alien story.

43
00:02:53,550 --> 00:02:56,066
This is a rain spirit, not a pilot.

44
00:02:56,533 --> 00:02:58,436
Room two: the Italian Alps.

45
00:02:58,436 --> 00:03:06,400
In Val Camonica, glaciers polished the bedrock smooth, and for thousands of years people hammered images into it.

46
00:03:06,866 --> 00:03:18,366
It is one of the largest collections of prehistoric rock art in the world, over one hundred forty thousand figures, and Italy's first UNESCO World Heritage Site.

47
00:03:18,833 --> 00:03:25,933
On one rock at Zurla, near Nadro, stand two figures with round, rayed heads, each holding an object.

48
00:03:25,933 --> 00:03:30,833
Since the nineteen sixties, they have had a nickname: the astronauts.

49
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:36,547
The theory says the rays are helmets with antennae, the objects instruments.

50
00:03:36,547 --> 00:03:40,000
Some websites even date them to eight thousand BC.

51
00:03:40,466 --> 00:03:42,719
Archaeologists see something else.

52
00:03:42,719 --> 00:03:51,400
Figures like these belong to the valley's late phase, roughly three thousand years ago, when the Camunni made most of the carvings.

53
00:03:51,866 --> 00:03:55,204
Rayed heads appear on many Camunian figures.

54
00:03:55,204 --> 00:04:04,233
Specialists read them as feathered or horned headdresses, solar symbols, or the radiance of gods and masked celebrants.

55
00:04:04,699 --> 00:04:09,220
Around them are duels, hunts, ploughing scenes, huts and maps.

56
00:04:09,220 --> 00:04:12,720
A world of farmers and warriors, drawn as ideas.

57
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:16,366
Nothing here flies, lands, or carries anyone away.

58
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:27,000
And popular photos often show the astronauts with their grooves filled in bright white, a modern addition that makes the outlines look crisp and helmet-like.

59
00:04:27,466 --> 00:04:28,835
Exhibit two verdict.

60
00:04:28,835 --> 00:04:33,625
Ritual figures with radiant heads, carved by the people of the valley.

61
00:04:33,625 --> 00:04:37,800
Space helmet is our word for a shape they already understood.

62
00:04:38,266 --> 00:04:41,100
Room three: a monastery in Kosovo.

63
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:49,433
Visoki Dečani, begun in thirteen twenty-seven, is by far the largest medieval church in the Balkans.

64
00:04:49,899 --> 00:04:53,616
Inside are more than a thousand fresco compositions.

65
00:04:53,616 --> 00:04:59,833
High on one wall is a Crucifixion, painted around the middle of the fourteenth century.

66
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:03,100
And this is the detail that went viral.

67
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:11,500
On each side of the cross, a teardrop-shaped object streaks across the sky, with a small human figure sitting inside.

68
00:05:11,966 --> 00:05:14,159
To ufologists, it is obvious.

69
00:05:14,159 --> 00:05:19,000
Two pilots in two capsules, watching the crucifixion from above.

70
00:05:19,466 --> 00:05:25,333
But crucifixion scenes almost always include two extra guests: the Sun and the Moon.

71
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:32,666
The Gospels say darkness covered the land, and artists showed the Sun and Moon mourning beside the cross.

72
00:05:33,133 --> 00:05:43,066
They appear as faces, busts, or figures riding inside the discs, a tradition reaching back to the sun and moon gods of Greek and Roman art.

73
00:05:43,533 --> 00:05:45,088
Look again at Dečani.

74
00:05:45,088 --> 00:05:51,160
The right-hand object is shaped like a crescent moon, and the streaks show motion.

75
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:57,233
Serbian art historians call it a standard Sun and Moon, painted in an unusual way.

76
00:05:57,699 --> 00:06:08,766
A twenty seventeen study in the journal Culture and Cosmos examined these exact images, and concluded the same: personifications of the Sun and the Moon.

77
00:06:09,233 --> 00:06:10,693
Exhibit three verdict.

78
00:06:10,693 --> 00:06:11,556
Not capsules.

79
00:06:11,556 --> 00:06:16,600
The Sun and the Moon, grieving at the cross, for nearly seven hundred years.

80
00:06:17,066 --> 00:06:25,466
Room four brings us back to Florence: the Palazzo Vecchio, and the painting known as the Madonna with Saint Giovannino.

81
00:06:25,933 --> 00:06:30,478
It is a round panel from around the year fifteen hundred.

82
00:06:30,478 --> 00:06:38,533
Even the painter is disputed: Jacopo del Sellaio, Sebastiano Mainardi, and online, often Ghirlandaio.

83
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:45,666
Over Mary's shoulder hangs the object: grey, oval, tilted, with rays around its rim.

84
00:06:45,666 --> 00:06:49,000
A man below raises a hand to his forehead.

85
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,666
His dog looks up too.

86
00:06:51,133 --> 00:06:54,533
For believers, this is the clearest case of all.

87
00:06:54,533 --> 00:07:01,333
A leaden craft over Tuscany, witnessed by a shepherd centuries before anyone said flying saucer.

88
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:04,350
Now read it as a Florentine would.

89
00:07:04,350 --> 00:07:07,875
A shepherd, a dog, a flock, a light in the sky.

90
00:07:07,875 --> 00:07:15,300
That is the Annunciation to the Shepherds, from Luke: the glory of the Lord shone round about them.

91
00:07:15,766 --> 00:07:21,066
Painters also used the Protevangelium of James, from the second century.

92
00:07:21,066 --> 00:07:26,955
A luminous cloud covers the Nativity cave, so bright the eyes could not bear it.

93
00:07:26,955 --> 00:07:29,899
That is why shepherds shield their eyes.

94
00:07:30,366 --> 00:07:31,761
And the grey colour?

95
00:07:31,761 --> 00:07:36,292
Close-up photographs show tiny fragments of gold leaf at the rim.

96
00:07:36,292 --> 00:07:41,033
On one reading, the cloud was once gilded, and the gold flaked away.

97
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:47,255
Bright outlined clouds carrying angels appear in countless religious paintings.

98
00:07:47,255 --> 00:07:53,666
In scripture, a cloud is how God's presence appears, from Exodus to the Transfiguration.

99
00:07:54,133 --> 00:07:55,775
Exhibit four verdict.

100
00:07:55,775 --> 00:07:59,293
An angel's luminous cloud that lost its gold.

101
00:07:59,293 --> 00:08:02,421
The shepherd is not filing a UFO report.

102
00:08:02,421 --> 00:08:04,766
He is hearing news of a birth.

103
00:08:05,233 --> 00:08:06,892
Room five is different.

104
00:08:06,892 --> 00:08:10,210
Not a religious painting, but a piece of news.

105
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:14,899
Nuremberg, at dawn on the fourteenth of April, fifteen sixty-one.

106
00:08:15,366 --> 00:08:22,332
A broadsheet by Hans Glaser reports that many men and women saw a dreadful apparition on the sun.

107
00:08:22,332 --> 00:08:26,066
The sheet survives in the Central Library of Zurich.

108
00:08:26,533 --> 00:08:33,194
It describes blood-red arcs, balls of black and iron colour, crosses, and tubes holding globes.

109
00:08:33,194 --> 00:08:38,733
They fought for over an hour, then fell to earth as if burning, in great smoke.

110
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:44,333
Ufologists call it the first recorded air battle between alien craft.

111
00:08:44,333 --> 00:08:50,433
Cylinders as mother ships, spheres as fighters, and a huge black spear at the end.

112
00:08:50,899 --> 00:08:53,758
But read it as a meteorologist would.

113
00:08:53,758 --> 00:09:02,874
Thin ice clouds, eight to ten kilometres up, can paint rings, arcs, bright sun dogs and crossing lines around the sun.

114
00:09:02,874 --> 00:09:04,033
A halo display.

115
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,214
Red arcs beside the sun.

116
00:09:06,214 --> 00:09:08,285
Coloured spots on both sides.

117
00:09:08,285 --> 00:09:10,214
Crosses where circles meet.

118
00:09:10,214 --> 00:09:15,500
And it happened at sunrise, with the sun low, where sun dogs often appear.

119
00:09:15,966 --> 00:09:17,659
The fit is not perfect.

120
00:09:17,659 --> 00:09:19,868
A woodcut is not a photograph.

121
00:09:19,868 --> 00:09:26,200
And the text ends like a sermon: whatever such signs mean, God alone knows, so repent.

122
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:33,387
Sheets of sky wonders, comets and multiple suns, were popular in sixteenth-century Germany.

123
00:09:33,387 --> 00:09:37,966
Each was read as a sign from God, not a report about aircraft.

124
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:39,974
Exhibit five verdict.

125
00:09:39,974 --> 00:09:45,697
A real sky event, most likely a halo display, filtered through fear and faith.

126
00:09:45,697 --> 00:09:47,238
People saw something.

127
00:09:47,238 --> 00:09:49,000
It just was not a fleet.

128
00:09:49,466 --> 00:09:50,519
Our last room.

129
00:09:50,519 --> 00:09:58,566
The Fitzwilliam Museum in Cambridge owns a small oil painting, made around seventeen ten by Aert de Gelder.

130
00:09:59,033 --> 00:10:06,700
De Gelder was one of Rembrandt's last pupils, and he carried Rembrandt's dark, glowing style into the eighteenth century.

131
00:10:07,166 --> 00:10:11,113
The Baptism of Christ shows John and Jesus by the water.

132
00:10:11,113 --> 00:10:17,033
Above them hangs a bright disc, and four beams of light shoot down onto the figures.

133
00:10:17,500 --> 00:10:23,100
The UFO reading: a silver saucer, beaming light down like a tractor beam.

134
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:27,166
It still appears in nearly every list of UFOs in art.

135
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:30,709
But the Gospels describe this moment plainly.

136
00:10:30,709 --> 00:10:34,605
The heavens opened, and the Spirit descended like a dove.

137
00:10:34,605 --> 00:10:39,799
And at the centre of the disc, a researcher found exactly that: a tiny dove.

138
00:10:40,266 --> 00:10:45,451
Opening heavens, rays and a dove are the standard way to paint the baptism.

139
00:10:45,451 --> 00:10:50,566
De Gelder simply painted it in Rembrandt's language of darkness and light.

140
00:10:51,033 --> 00:10:52,474
Exhibit six verdict.

141
00:10:52,474 --> 00:10:55,788
The Holy Spirit as a dove in a burst of light.

142
00:10:55,788 --> 00:11:00,399
The saucer is the sky opening, exactly as the text describes it.

143
00:11:00,866 --> 00:11:03,104
So why do these images fool us?

144
00:11:03,104 --> 00:11:11,766
Because we bring our own picture of a flying saucer, born in nineteen forty-seven, and lay it over art made long before.

145
00:11:12,233 --> 00:11:15,707
Every exhibit had a meaning in its own time.

146
00:11:15,707 --> 00:11:16,813
A rain spirit.

147
00:11:16,813 --> 00:11:18,076
A ritual figure.

148
00:11:18,076 --> 00:11:19,419
The Sun and Moon.

149
00:11:19,419 --> 00:11:20,761
An angel's cloud.

150
00:11:20,761 --> 00:11:22,183
A frightening sky.

151
00:11:22,183 --> 00:11:22,736
A dove.

152
00:11:22,736 --> 00:11:25,500
Not one was described as a machine.

153
00:11:25,966 --> 00:11:27,328
And there is a cost.

154
00:11:27,328 --> 00:11:37,133
Calling these works alien takes them away from the people who made them: Aboriginal artists, Alpine farmers, Serbian monks, Florentine painters.

155
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,033
The gallery is closed.

156
00:11:39,033 --> 00:11:40,466
Here is the scorecard.

157
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:45,291
Wandjina as helmeted visitors: debunked, rain spirits.

158
00:11:45,291 --> 00:11:49,327
Val Camonica astronauts: debunked, ritual figures.

159
00:11:49,327 --> 00:11:52,878
Dečani capsules: debunked, the Sun and Moon.

160
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:56,833
The Madonna's object: debunked, an angel's cloud.

161
00:11:57,299 --> 00:12:01,674
Nuremberg: partly explained, most likely a halo display.

162
00:12:01,674 --> 00:12:04,564
De Gelder's saucer: debunked, a dove.

163
00:12:04,564 --> 00:12:07,533
Any of the six meant as a craft: none.

164
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:08,901
The verdict.

165
00:12:08,901 --> 00:12:16,034
Six famous UFOs in art, and six works that make sense once you read them in their own language.

166
00:12:16,034 --> 00:12:21,966
The only real unknown was Nuremberg's sky, and even that has a natural suspect.

167
00:12:22,433 --> 00:12:24,908
That does not make the sky boring.

168
00:12:24,908 --> 00:12:30,661
People have always turned what they saw above them into gods, omens and angels.

169
00:12:30,661 --> 00:12:35,466
That instinct is the real treasure here, and it is entirely human.

170
00:12:35,933 --> 00:12:41,134
So next time you spot a saucer in an old painting, ask our three questions.

171
00:12:41,134 --> 00:12:44,533
The answer is usually more beautiful than aliens.

172
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,288
That is the gallery.

173
00:12:46,288 --> 00:12:48,672
Which exhibit fooled you the longest?

174
00:12:48,672 --> 00:12:53,633
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery on trial.
